{"signature": "{\"model\": \"eleven_multilingual_v2\", \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\", \"settings\": {\"similarity_boost\": 0.85, \"stability\": 0.5, \"style\": 0.0, \"use_speaker_boost\": true}, \"text\": \"When you lift an object, you do work against the force of gravity. Energy is transferred to the object's gravitational potential energy store. When the object falls, its gravitational potential energy store decreases and, if we ignore air resistance, its kinetic energy store increases by the same amount. The equation is: change in gravitational potential energy equals mass multiplied by gravitational field strength multiplied by change in vertical height. In symbols, delta E sub p equals m times g times delta h. Mass is measured in kilograms, gravitational field strength in newtons per kilogram, height in metres and energy in joules.\", \"voice\": \"28e9d9dcea90e5b4\"}", "duration": 42.527347, "words": [["When", 0.0], ["you", 0.29], ["lift", 0.476], ["an", 0.766], ["object,", 0.894], ["you", 1.324], ["do", 1.498], ["work", 1.695], ["against", 1.997], ["the", 2.345], ["force", 2.473], ["of", 2.798], ["gravity.", 2.926], ["Energy", 3.657], ["is", 4.214], ["transferred", 4.365], ["to", 4.923], ["the", 5.027], ["object's", 5.166], ["gravitational", 5.666], ["potential", 6.478], ["energy", 7.082], ["store.", 7.546], ["When", 8.173], ["the", 8.429], ["object", 8.591], ["falls,", 9.056], ["its", 9.578], ["gravitational", 9.822], ["potential", 10.565], ["energy", 11.122], ["store", 11.529], ["decreases", 11.854], ["and,", 12.539], ["if", 13.177], ["we", 13.375], ["ignore", 13.538], ["air", 13.979], ["resistance,", 14.258], ["its", 15.186], ["kinetic", 15.453], ["energy", 16.034], ["store", 16.463], ["increases", 16.905], ["by", 17.508], ["the", 17.706], ["same", 17.857], ["amount.", 18.158], ["The", 18.809], ["equation", 18.971], ["is:", 19.528], ["change", 19.935], ["in", 20.388], ["gravitational", 20.55], ["potential", 21.328], ["energy", 21.932], ["equals", 22.675], ["